    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Polished concrete offers exceptional durability with minimal maintenance, resistant to heavy impacts and chemical spills, though it can feel cold and requires sealing to prevent staining. Luxury vinyl tile provides similar water and stain resistance with comfortable aesthetics underfoot, but it may wear slower on extreme abrasion compared to stone or concrete over many years. Natural stone like granite or slate delivers a premium, timeless look with high hardness, yet it demands regular resealing and professional polishing to maintain its appearance against constant foot traffic. For a high-traffic law firm in London, polished concrete often presents the most cost-effective and low-maintenance solution in the long run. Consider a mixed approach using these materials strategically to balance budget, tactile comfort for staff, and the firm's desired brand image.",
